[Account Abuse Protection](/bots/account-abuse-protection/) now shows when a recognized AI assistant makes a login or sign up request, and which account it was acting for.

- **Population overview**: See which AI assistants are active across your users and how many accounts use them.
- **Account activity**: Every login and sign up event shows whether an AI assistant made the request, and which one.
- **AI assistant filters**: filter accounts by number of AI assistant events or number of AI assistants.

Use this to investigate and mitigate a single account without blocking an assistant for everyone else who relies on it, and to tune your agent settings in [AI Crawler and Agent access policies](/bots/additional-configurations/block-ai-bots/).

AI assistant visibility covers login and sign up events only. Requests from assistants that Cloudflare does not recognize appear as ordinary traffic.

For more information, refer to [AI assistants](/bots/account-abuse-protection/#ai-assistants).
